<!-- Aura-SOC - rule 100668 (level 7). Domain: threat_hunting,linux,mitre_gaps,
     Naming convention and load-order trap: see rules/README.md -->
<group name="threat_hunting,linux,mitre_gaps,">

  <!-- Fix 3 (2026-08-09), purple-team finding: 100658 (burst, 12 cmd/30s) is
       the ONLY correlation guarding discovery commands. A purple-team run
       against debian2/debian3 ran T1082+T1033+T1007 one command at a time,
       >30s apart, specifically to stay under 100658 - zero alert of any kind
       was produced (below that, individual matches sit at level 3, see 100657/
       100667, well under nothing suspicious on their own).

       This rule is the gap-closer: same host-wide correlation as 100658 (see
       its comment - <same_field>audit.auid</same_field> does not fire in this
       Wazuh version, so this is host-wide too, not per-user), but a longer
       window and lower count catches paced/manual enumeration that a burst
       counter structurally cannot.

       REVERTED to frequency=5/timeframe=600 (2026-08-09, same day): an
       intermediate version raised this to 8/300s to tolerate a login-time
       false positive, traced at the time to Debian's update-motd.d. Checking
       the agent's raw /var/log/audit/audit.log directly showed the real
       source was pam_systemd (systemctl user-session env setup, session
       plumbing, fires on every login on any systemd host) - not MOTD at all.
       Fixed properly at the source in 100669 (exclusion by if_sid, matching
       audit.execve.a1/a2 exactly), so this rule no longer needs desensitizing
       to survive normal login traffic. Left permanently weakened it would
       have missed slower/quieter real recon than intended.

       Level 7 (MEDIUM): distinguishable from the level-3 baseline and from the
       level-10 burst, but deliberately short of HIGH - this is a pattern
       worth an analyst's attention, not a confirmed compromise. -->

  <rule id="100668" level="7" frequency="5" timeframe="600">
    <if_matched_group>discovery_baseline</if_matched_group>
    <description>Paced system discovery (5+ discovery commands over 10 min) - reconnaissance below the burst threshold</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1082</id>
      <id>T1033</id>
      <id>T1057</id>
      <id>T1007</id>
      <id>T1016</id>
      <id>T1018</id>
      <id>T1049</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
